A||||4||Wannabe||Northstar "No Good"???||||4||
Z||000000||Wannabe||08-20-2001||09:36 AM||||My cousin works in one of the larger local Cadillace delaerships in the service department. When discussing my plans for a Northstar swap, he cautioned that Northstars, especially the STS 300HP version, are notorious for major oil leaks and high oil consumption, like 2 liters every 1000 miles.According to him, almost 3/4 of the Northstars that come through the shop have these problems. He has no reason to lie about this, but I wonder if the problem looks worse that it is because the service department is going to see most of the bad ones and not many of the good ones. Has anybpody else heard or seen anything about this?||||reg||4
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||08-20-2001||10:39 AM||||I have a mechanic friend who states that the Northstars have sealant problems, but not until AT LEAST 100k miles or more.  As for your cadillac dealer-guy.  I guess it's possible that half of the serviced cars have those troubles, but how many people don't bring their Northstar Caddy there for service- if it isn't leaking, why bring it in for service?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig2.jpg">    <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000002||KissMySSFiero||08-20-2001||02:03 PM||||i worked at a cadi dealer for about a year.  i never saw one that consumed that much oil.  on problem they did have was blown head gasket.  but not on a low milage engine.  Nstar is a great engine.  why do you think they havent revised anything on it since it came out.  a 93 nstar is the same as a 2000.  the earlier ones are obd-I and later obd-II thats about it.  but nothing mechanical has changed.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||08-20-2001||02:09 PM||||Actually, they got essentially new heads in 2000.  and a reduction in compression from 10.3 to 10.0:1 combined to allow the engine to burn 87 octane instead of premium (typical american thinking, I'd have bumped it to 11:1 and kept the premium fuel  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But that's about it, the engine has remained essentially unchanged in the bottom end, as far as I can tell, for the last 9 years.<P>It has a reputation for being bulletproof, the cadilac LMP race car uses a stock block and bearings, etc.  it does get new internals for a 4.0l displacement with turbos though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (and "600+" horsepower.  theh 'plus' is anyone's guess.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The 93 year had head gasket problems, it's actually fameous for it, and cadicac replaced most of them.  Ater they switched gasket types, the engine is actually reliable! woah!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>i worked at a cadi dealer for about a year.  i never saw one that consumed that much oil.  on problem they did have was blown head gasket.  but not on a low milage engine.  Nstar is a great engine.  why do you think they havent revised anything on it since it came out.  a 93 nstar is the same as a 2000.  the earlier ones are obd-I and later obd-II thats about it.  but nothing mechanical has changed.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||Wannabe||08-20-2001||03:51 PM||||Strange how different people see different things. I had never heard anything substantially bad about the Northstar until my cousin's story. It always makes sense to listen to more than one opinion.||||reg||1
